   It also changes uv.lock:
     · databricks-sql-connector 4.3.0 → 4.9.0
     · yarl 1.22.0 → 1.25.1
     · pydantic-settings 2.16.3 (added)

   Dependabot resolves for the oldest Python requires-python allows (3.11) and filters out releases that need a newer one: soupsieve 4.1.3 needs Python >=3.11.5. uv locks them only for the Pythons they support.

   Verified with uv's resolver: all fixes resolve together.
   Then run: uv lock --upgrade-package aiohttp==3.14.4 --upgrade-package anyio==4.14.2 --upgrade-package certifi==2026.10.18 --upgrade-package cryptography==50.0.0 --upgrade-package dnspython==2.9.2 --upgrade-package filelock==4.2.1 --upgrade-package fsspec==2026.6.0 --upgrade-package litellm==1.100.4 --upgrade-package multidict==6.9.1 --upgrade-package oauthlib==4.0.1 --upgrade-package pyasn1==0.6.5 --upgrade-package pyjwt==2.15.0 --upgrade-package pymongo==4.18.3 --upgrade-package setuptools==84.1.0 --upgrade-package soupsieve --upgrade-package thrift==0.24.0 --upgrade-package urllib3==2.8.0 --upgrade-package werkzeug==3.1.9
